# NGINX-PROXY-BUFFERS: server-block fragment for the reverse proxy that sits in
# front of the Myrmidon board. The fork ships no nginx config (the production
# proxy lives outside this repository); this file is an example the board
# operator merges into the real server block.
#
# Why: agent wakes embed the issue list (GET /api/companies/:id/issues). Before
# AGENT-ISSUE-LIST the default answer was the full projection, easily above the
# nginx default proxy buffers (proxy_buffer_size 4k/8k), which forced nginx to
# spill answer headers/bodies to disk and logged "upstream response is buffered
# to ...". The agent default answer is now compact and <= 500 KB, but individual
# endpoints (issue detail, compact pages with descriptions) still return 64 KB+
# bodies, so the proxy buffers must be sized for them.
#
# Usage: copy the three directives into the `location /` block that proxies to
# the board service (upstream `myrmidon` in the production naming), then
# `nginx -t && nginx -s reload`. Values follow the ticket recommendation:
# proxy_buffer_size holds one header block (64k covers the largest response
# headers + a small body chunk), proxy_buffers holds the buffered body
# (16 x 64k = 1 MiB), proxy_busy_buffers_size may exceed one buffer while the
# rest flushes to the client.

# --- begin fragment (merge into the existing server/location block) ---
    proxy_buffer_size 64k;
    proxy_buffers 16 64k;
    proxy_busy_buffers_size 128k;
# --- end fragment ---
